            <div class="text-slate-700 text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed space-y-4">
              <p>
                When booking either format, consider how you want to get there:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
                <li><strong>Shared Coach Tour:</strong> The cheapest option, but expect 45 to 60 minutes spent driving around town picking up guests, plus potential commercial craft stops.</li>
                <li><strong>Small Group Minivan:</strong> A good middle ground with 8 to 12 passengers and quicker pickup.</li>
                <li><strong>Independent DIY via Grab / Ride-Hailing:</strong> A viable DIY option for couples or friends. Fares shift based on pickup location and demand. Return availability can be tricky outside the city, as fewer drivers want to head back toward town. For city sightseeing, pairing a morning trip with the <a href="/saigon-hop-on-hop-off-bus-guide" class="text-amber-800 hover:text-amber-900 font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 decoration-amber-300">Saigon hop-on hop-off bus</a> works well.</li>
                <li><strong>Public Bus:</strong> Possible for budget travelers via local buses, though it takes multiple transfers and 2.5 to 3 hours each way.</li>
                <li><strong>Private Car & Guide:</strong> The most flexible option. Direct hotel pickup, your choice of Ben Dinh or Ben Duoc, zero forced shopping stops, and you set your own pace.</li>
